<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74002" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνειαρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰτος</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, τό</span> (later perh.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνεαρ</span></b>  disyll.,
		v. infr. <i><span class="en">
			1.4
		</span></i>), 
			Ep.
		 word, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which
				brings profit, advantage,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				22.486
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				822
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέγα στιβάδεσσιν ὄνειαρ</span>
			<i>boon</i> for leafy couches, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				13.34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>means of strengthening, refreshment,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.444
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.78
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				41
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> in pl.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνείᾰτα,</span>
			<i>food, victuals,</i> freq. in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (esp. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>) in the line 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δ᾽ ἐπ᾽ ὀνείαθ᾽ ἑτοῖμα προκείμενα
					χεῖρας ἴαλλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.149
				</span></i>
			. al. ; also of <i>rich presents,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοσσάδ᾽ ὀνείατ᾽ ἄγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.367
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> of persons,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶσιν ὄ.,</span> of Hector, <i><span class="en">
				22.433
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῆμα κακὸς γείτων, ὅσσον τ᾽ ἀγαθὸς
					μέγ᾽ ὄ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					346
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθανάτοις θνητοῖσί τ᾽
				ὄνεα&lt;&gt;ρ καὶ χάρμα τέτυκται,</span> of
			Demeter, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Cer.</u>
				269
			</span></i> (cj. Ilgen, for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνειαρ</span>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄναρ</span> (v. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄναρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1.1
				</span></i>
			 fin., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνειρος</span> I),
				<i>dream,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὐμὸν ὄ. ἐμοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Epigr.</u>
					49
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				7.42
			</span></i>. (The true spelling in early 
				Ion.
			 is prob. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνηαρ,</span> which
			is called 
				Aeol.
			 by <i><span class="en">
				Choerob.
			</span></i> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				2.245
			</span></i> : hence later 
				Ion.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνέᾱρ</span> : prob. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀνᾱϝαρ,</span> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνίνημι.</span>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
